# Functional test: a commit that sets dscp-map 46 on a peer of a daemon running the
# Linux XFRM dataplane is refused, and the operator is told why and how to fix it.
# Spec: plan/release/fixes/spec-rfc4301-architecture-gaps.md (RFC 4301 Section
#       5.1.2.1 note 5). The dataplane-independent half (copy, 0 and 63 accepted; 64
#       and a value on a transport-mode peer refused) is test/parse/ipsec-dscp-map.ci,
#       and the accepted values reaching the kernel is ipsec-sa-options-kernel.ci.
#
# RFC 4301 Section 5.1.2.1 note 5: "If the packet will immediately enter a domain for
# which the DSCP value in the outer header is not appropriate, that value MUST be
# mapped to an appropriate value for the domain".
#
# VALIDATES: the backend half of config verify. xfrm4_tunnel_encap_add copies the
#            inner DS field, or writes 0 under XFRM_SA_XFLAG_DONT_ENCAP_DSCP, and
#            nothing else, so Linux XFRM cannot write 46. The ike plugin's
#            OnConfigVerify (engine/register.go) calls verifyPeerSAOptions
#            (engine/sa_options.go), which asks the loaded backend
#            (dataplane/xfrm_linux.go SAOptionsSupported -> xfrmDSCPFlag) and refuses
#            the commit with the backend's message: the field, the reason and the
#            fix. The reload reaches it as an operator's commit does.
# PREVENTS: a mapped DSCP silently installed as a copy or as 0, which marks every
#           tunnel packet with a class the operator's domain did not ask for, and a
#           refusal deferred to the Child SA install, which leaves a peer that
#           commits and never carries traffic.
#
# WHY A RELOAD AND NOT A START. Config verify judges a commit; the configuration a
# daemon starts with is applied without it (dataplane.ErrSAOptionRefused states it),
# so a start with dscp-map 46 would test the install-time refusal instead. The
# daemon starts with the peer at the default and the staged fixture
# (reload/live-stages) reloads the same file with dscp-map 46 added.
#
# WHY NO TUNNEL. The verify judges the configuration against the loaded backend
# before any Child SA exists, so the peer is connection-type respond and nobody
# initiates. It is there only to carry the leaf.
#
# WHY THE FILE IS ze-bgp. Only a command whose binary is `ze` gets its `-` replaced
# by a config file and writes daemon.pid, and the live-stages `reload` step copies
# its source over ze-bgp.conf (ipsec-peer-reload-applies-selectors.ci). The plugin
# block is byte-identical in both configs, so the reload keeps the fixture alive.
#
# RED PROOF: in internal/component/ike/dataplane/xfrm_linux.go xfrmDSCPFlag, replace
# the closing `return false, fmt.Errorf("%w: outer DSCP %d cannot be expressed ...`
# with `return true, nil` (46 accepted and installed as 0). The reload commits, no
# refusal is logged, and both refusal expectations fail. A second break, deleting
# the `verifyPeerSAOptions` call from OnConfigVerify in engine/register.go, does the
# same.
#
# Gated option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf: the daemon loads the real xfrm
# backend, which is the one whose refusal this is (the noop backend accepts every
# option), so this SKIPs on a host without CAP_NET_ADMIN and runs as root in the
# QEMU VM, where `fsuite ipsec` in internal/le/test/qemu/alltests.go executes it.

# bpf: the default `vpn ipsec application-override deny` loads a cgroup setsockopt guard.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf
# Serialize against every other real-XFRM ipsec test: the SPD is NODE-WIDE, and the
# daemon installs its IKE bypass and catch-all there.
option=exclusive:group=ipsec-xfrm
option=env:var=ze_test_ike_port:value=$PORT2
option=timeout:value=60s

# The configuration the operator commits: the start configuration plus dscp-map 46.
tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONFIG2
plugin {
	external live-stages {
		run "le test fixture reload/live-stages stages.script"
		encoder json
	}
}

vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		esp-group esp-default {
			lifetime 3600
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		ike-group ike-default {
			key-exchange ikev2
			lifetime 28800
			proposal 1 {
				dh-group 14
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		site-to-site {
			peer idle {
				ike-group ike-default
				esp-group esp-default
				connection-type respond
				local-address 127.0.0.2
				remote-address 127.0.0.1
				mode tunnel
				dscp-map 46
				traffic-selector 1 {
					local {
						prefix 198.18.250.0/24
					}
					remote {
						prefix 198.18.251.0/24
					}
				}
				authentication {
					mode pre-shared-secret
					pre-shared-secret test-key-1234
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG2

tmpfs=stages.script:terminator=EOF_SCRIPT
reload config2.conf
say DSCP-MAP-RELOAD-PROCESSED
EOF_SCRIPT

# ── The daemon (REAL xfrm): the start configuration, peer at the default dscp-map ──
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external live-stages {
		run "le test fixture reload/live-stages stages.script"
		encoder json
	}
}

vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		esp-group esp-default {
			lifetime 3600
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		ike-group ike-default {
			key-exchange ikev2
			lifetime 28800
			proposal 1 {
				dh-group 14
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		site-to-site {
			peer idle {
				ike-group ike-default
				esp-group esp-default
				connection-type respond
				local-address 127.0.0.2
				remote-address 127.0.0.1
				mode tunnel
				traffic-selector 1 {
					local {
						prefix 198.18.250.0/24
					}
					remote {
						prefix 198.18.251.0/24
					}
				}
				authentication {
					mode pre-shared-secret
					pre-shared-secret test-key-1234
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# The fixture's last step passes, then it asks the daemon to shut down cleanly.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=55s

# The reload was processed (the reload-status generation advanced) and refused with
# the backend's reason and fix.
expect=stderr:contains=DSCP-MAP-RELOAD-PROCESSED
expect=stderr:contains=outer DSCP 46 cannot be expressed
expect=stderr:contains=configure dscp-map copy or 0 on this peer
reject=stderr:pattern=LIVE-STAGES line
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
reject=stderr:pattern=fatal error
